course: dictionary
lesson: 9458
title: Stare and the meaning of a look
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To stare means to look at someone or something for a long time without looking away. A stare is the long, fixed look itself. «She stared at the floor and would not talk.» The words around stare tell you she was not looking up or around: she was fixed on one spot.
explain: Context can also show you how a stare feels to the person being stared at. «At the birthday they stood round the trampoline staring at their trainers.» Here the children are shy, and staring at their feet helps them avoid talking. Staring is not always rude, but it can make someone uncomfortable.
explain: Stare is a verb and a noun. «Josh stares at the clock» uses it as a verb, and «She gave him a long stare» uses it as a noun. Watch for the small ending: stares, stared and staring are all forms of the same verb. Try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: To stare means to look at something for a long time without looking away.
fact: A stare is a long, fixed look.
fact: Phrases to know: stare at, stare into space, stare back, and a blank stare.
fact: Staring at people, especially someone who looks different or has a disability, can make them uncomfortable. It is polite to look away or smile and say hello.
fact: Never stare at the Sun, not even with sunglasses, because it can damage your eyes.
exercise: «He stared at the clock until the bell rang.» What does stare mean? | To close your eyes tightly | To laugh loudly | *To look at something for a long time without looking away | To run quickly away
exercise: Mia gave her brother a long stare across the table. What is a stare? | A kind hug | A loud shout | *A long, fixed look | A quick wave
exercise: «It can make someone uncomfortable to be stared at.» What is the polite thing to do? | Stand closer to watch | Stare back until they leave | Point and whisper to a friend | *Look away or smile and say hello
test: «Never stare at the Sun, not even with sunglasses.» Why must you never do this? | Sunglasses are not allowed outside | It helps you blink less | It makes the Sun shine brighter | *It can damage your eyes
test: «Staring at screens makes you blink less, so eyes get dry and tired.» What does this tell you? | *Staring at a screen can make your eyes feel dry | Blinking is bad for your eyes | Screens make your eyes stronger | Dry eyes are a sign you are happy
exam: Why should you not stare at a strange dog? | It will copy your look and bark | *It may see your stare as a threat | It will want to play with you | It will fall asleep straight away
